WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.438
Microsoft's D L P templates are a
convenient start and a poor design.

2
00:00:04.438 --> 00:00:09.288
The program writes each policy from an
outcome statement the policy owner owns.

3
00:00:09.288 --> 00:00:14.357
For example: content labeled C U I isn't
shared or sent outside the tenant except

4
00:00:14.357 --> 00:00:18.024
through the approved partner
path; an attempt is blocked,

5
00:00:18.024 --> 00:00:21.612
the user is told why, and the
security monitor is alerted.

6
00:00:21.612 --> 00:00:25.438
Rules match labels first, a
decision someone already made,

7
00:00:25.438 --> 00:00:28.626
and treat raw content
patterns as the safety net.

8
00:00:28.626 --> 00:00:33.526
Overrides are logged and read every
week, and exceptions name groups,

9
00:00:33.526 --> 00:00:36.450
sit in a register, and
expire within a year.

10
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:43.262
Endpoint D L P covers Windows 10 and
11, and Windows Server 2019 and later.

11
00:00:43.262 --> 00:00:48.274
For content nobody labeled, auto-labeling
climbs a ladder: built-in types,

12
00:00:48.274 --> 00:00:52.366
custom types, exact data match,
then trainable classifiers,

13
00:00:52.366 --> 00:00:55.038
only as far as false positives require.

14
00:00:55.038 --> 00:00:59.102
Client-side labeling recommends
a label while the author works;

15
00:00:59.102 --> 00:01:02.476
service-side labeling applies
one at rest and in mail.

16
00:01:02.476 --> 00:01:04.865
In GCC, D L P on every surface,

17
00:01:04.865 --> 00:01:10.250
auto-labeling and exact data
match are listed as available.
